error[E1013]: `xs` is being iterated, so it cannot be lent `mut`
 --> mem:///main.lu:6:9
  |
5 |     for x in xs {
  |              -- the `for` loop holds `xs` from here, for its whole extent
6 |         (mut xs).push(x)
  |         ^^^^^^^^ the container changes under the loop
  |
  = note: iterating holds a read claim on the container for the loop's extent [mem.iter.excl].
    Collect the changes into a second list and apply them after the loop — or use an index
    loop (`var i = 0` … `while i < xs.len`), whose condition re-reads the length every pass.
